# Rover P4 110 four-door saloon, 1962-1964.
#
# The last and most powerful P4, with the 2.6-litre six in high tune and the
# 1962 grille. It closed the P4 range in 1964.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rover_P4
#
# Dimensions: variant-specific overall figures were not established; the
# family wheelbase is 2.819 m.
#
# Shape reference: a true level profile, identified by the wing script and the
# Commons title, with front and rear three-quarters.
#
# Colours: grade (b), the P4 Drivers Guild's year-based compilation. Black,
# Sage Green, Dove Grey and Maroon. Weights 6, 5, 5, 4, total 20, provisional.
#
# Speed 160 km/h. Comfort 68/282, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 68. Classes 3,4.
# Dates are road presence: 1962 intro, retires staggered 1980-1983.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/rover-p4-110.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/rover-p4-110.dae. References:
# citycars/references/rover-p4-110/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the grille does not reproduce the distinct divided
# appearance of the late nose, and the rear glass and wing shoulders are too
# flat. At 128 px the 1962 grille, lamps and P4 body read as a P4 110.


obj=citycar
name=RoverP4110(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=6
intro_year=1962
intro_month=9
retire_year=1983
retire_month=6
speed=160
class=3,4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=68
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=282

